{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_correction_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_correction_neg","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L64-L77","doc":"**Sign of the missing L2 term (conditional on the EM-Coulomb model).**\nIf the electromagnetic correction to `Δm = m_n − m_p` is\n`δ = -k·(Σqq(proton) − Σqq(neutron))` for any positive self-energy coupling\n`k > 0` (the standard Coulomb self-energy, higher energy ⇒ heavier ⇒ subtracts\nfrom `m_n − m_p`), then `δ < 0`.\n\nCombined with the traced-volume leading piece **over**-predicting `Δm`\n(residual `< 0`), the EM correction has the **right sign** to close the gap.\nThis constrains any candidate closure: it must be charge-odd and reduce `Δm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L60-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_gap_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_gap_eq","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L54-L58","doc":"**Charge-structure gap.** `Σqq(proton) − Σqq(neutron) = +1/3 > 0`: the\nproton carries the larger Coulomb self-energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure_udd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure_udd","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L50-L52","doc":"Neutron `udd`: the Coulomb charge-structure factor is `-1/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure_uud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure_uud","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Proton `uud`: the Coulomb charge-structure factor vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.chargeStructure","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The pairwise Coulomb charge-structure factor `Σ_{i<j} q_i q_j` of a\nthree-quark ordering `(c₀, c₁, c₂)` — the leading electromagnetic\nself-energy weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.qDown","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.qDown","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L38-L39","doc":"Electric charge of the down quark (units of `e`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.qUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.qUp","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/NeutronProtonEMSign.lean#L35-L36","doc":"Electric charge of the up quark (units of `e`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}